    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0910" n="900" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg900"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.243/10–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-22T10:00:00+09:00">October 22,
                            1947—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 21—11:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2112. Minister of Communications<anchor n="80" xml:id="d700-f1"/> has made
                    request to Ambassador that spare parts et cetera in group program be sold by FLC
                    to Ministry at 10 cents on dollar (refEmbtel 1902, September 14 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">11</hi>], 4 p.m.) Col. Ivy of FLC is informing
                    Washington further regarding his discussions with Ministry.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d700-f1" n="80" xml:id="d700-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Yu Ta-wei.</p>
